# Patient Voice for Quality Care

**Practical tools and evidence-informed resources to collect, analyse, and use patient experience feedback to improve healthcare quality and patient-centred care.**

## About This Project

Patient Voice for Quality Care is an open resource initiative designed to help healthcare professionals, quality improvement teams, health system leaders, and healthcare organisations understand and use patients' experiences to improve the quality of care.

Patients are not merely recipients of healthcare services. Their experiences, perspectives, concerns, and feedback provide valuable insights into the safety, effectiveness, responsiveness, accessibility, and person-centredness of healthcare.

This repository aims to translate patient feedback into actionable learning and sustainable quality improvement.

## Why Patient Voice Matters

Healthcare quality cannot be fully understood through clinical indicators and service statistics alone. Listening to patients helps healthcare organisations identify gaps that routine data may overlook.

Meaningful patient engagement can help organisations:

- Understand patients' experiences throughout their care journey.
- Identify communication, access, dignity, respect, and responsiveness issues.
- Recognise opportunities to improve patient safety and service delivery.
- Use patient feedback to inform quality improvement priorities.
- Strengthen trust, accountability, and patient-centred care.
- Close the feedback loop by communicating what has changed.

## Objectives

This repository aims to:

1. Provide practical tools for collecting patient experience feedback.
2. Support the use of Patient-Reported Experience Measures (PREMs).
3. Help healthcare teams analyse and interpret patient feedback.
4. Translate patient concerns and complaints into improvement opportunities.
5. Support the integration of patient voice into healthcare quality improvement initiatives.
6. Encourage evidence-informed, ethical, and meaningful patient engagement.

